# What each of Polish's own characters arrives as: the code point a caller
# writes, and the byte its alphabet knows that character by. The bytes are the
# ones lang-alphabet.py put the letters at, which were free in the alphabet
# Italian brought; tools/lang-alphabet.py show plpl says what each one is now.

0105 82   # a with ogonek
0107 83   # c with acute
0119 84   # e with ogonek
0142 86   # l with stroke
0144 87   # n with acute
015b 88   # s with acute
017a 89   # z with acute
017c 8b   # z with dot above

# And the capitals, which arrive as their own lowercase. Nothing in the module
# lowercases them: convert_to_lowercase is a chain of 62 arms, one per letter it
# knows, and each arm plants the tag of the next, so adding eight means
# renumbering the chain. Until that is done a capital of Polish's own would
# reach the letter rules unconverted and be silent -- Żaba said aba, and ŁÓDŹ,
# being nothing but silent letters, crashed. Arriving lowercase is right for
# every sound and wrong only for anything that would want to know a letter was
# capital, which nothing here does yet.
0104 82   # A with ogonek, as a with ogonek
0106 83   # C with acute
0118 84   # E with ogonek
0141 86   # L with stroke
0143 87   # N with acute
015a 88   # S with acute
0179 89   # Z with acute
017b 8b   # Z with dot above
